flowchart LR
  %% Kryvos; CCS 2022, 15-page author version
  %% Evidence: https://publ.sec.uni-stuttgart.de/huberkuesterskripsliedtkemuellerrauschreisert-ccs-2022.pdf
  S1["Initialization<br/>Fix CRS, commitments, encryption keys"]
  S2["Registration<br/>Publish voters and authenticated channels"]
  S1 --> S2
  S3["Ballot generation<br/>Share vote; commit; encrypt openings; prove"]
  S2 --> S3
  S4["Validation and accumulation<br/>Weed ballots; sum public commitments"]
  S3 --> S4
  S5["Final tally<br/>Talliers reconstruct aggregate openings and tally"]
  S4 --> S5
  S6["Disclosure<br/>Publish result and tally-opening SNARK"]
  S5 --> S6
  %% Execution: Public board and private tallier exchange.
  %% Keys: Each tallier has an encryption key.
  %% Full tally: Talliers learn full tally; public learns result.
  %% Public checks: Commitment sums and result SNARK.
